        '0.53': "Arjuna said: O Keśava, what is the description of one of steady wisdom, established in samādhi? How does one of steady mind speak, how does he sit, how does he move?",
        '0.54': "The Blessed Lord said: When one gives up all desires arising in the mind, O Pārtha, and is content in the self by the self, then he is called one of steady wisdom.",
        '0.55': "One whose mind is not shaken in sorrow, who has no craving for pleasures, and who is free from attachment, fear and anger, is called a sage of steady mind.",
        '0.56': "He who is without attachment everywhere, who neither rejoices at obtaining good nor hates obtaining evil — his wisdom is firmly established.",
        '0.57': "When, like a tortoise drawing in its limbs on all sides, one withdraws the senses from their objects, his wisdom is firmly established.",
