        '0.67': "Therefore, O mighty-armed, he whose senses are completely restrained from their objects — his wisdom is firmly established.",
        '0.68': "What is night for all beings, in that the self-controlled one is awake; that in which beings are awake is night for the sage who sees.",
        '0.69': "As waters enter the ocean, which is ever being filled yet remains steady within its bounds, so he into whom all desires enter attains peace — not one who craves desires.",
